2026-08-05 14:20:00  Case 01-CONJUGATE start. Solver: codex/conjugate-bush, bush_thermal_model = CONDUCTION_2D.
2026-08-05 14:20:00  Pre-run findings, measured before the campaign and NOT worked around:
2026-08-05 14:20:00  (1) Newton linearisation of the wall term. Three choices for dT_b/dT_bar were
2026-08-05 14:20:00      implemented and measured at 720 x 192. The bore admittance with neighbouring
2026-08-05 14:20:00      bush cells frozen gives dT_b/dT_bar = 0.053 but scales with bush_radial_cells;
2026-08-05 14:20:00      the series-to-ambient conductance zeroes the wall coefficient and the
2026-08-05 14:20:00      temperature KSP DIVERGED at eps=0.60 psi=-40 (outer_robin80); a frozen bush
2026-08-05 14:20:00      (dT_b/dT_bar = 0) is mesh-free, matches the admittance answer to 5%, and runs.
2026-08-05 14:20:00      The frozen-bush form is what this campaign uses.
2026-08-05 14:20:00  (2) At 720 x 192 the outer_robin80 Picard loop LIMIT-CYCLES instead of meeting
2026-08-05 14:20:00      coupling_tolerance = 1e-6. R_p = 1.06e-3 / 9.83e-4 / 9.73e-4 at 100 / 200 / 400
2026-08-05 14:20:00      outer iterations (flat), i.e. ~100 Pa and ~8 mK of ripple per iteration.
2026-08-05 14:20:00      The SOLUTION is settled: W = 4013.431 N, p_max = 1.293835 MPa, T_max = 45.818 C,
2026-08-05 14:20:00      T_bearing peak 45.398 C @ 265.8 deg, torque 2.71739 N m -- identical to 6
2026-08-05 14:20:00      significant figures at 100, 200 and 400 iterations (eps 0.593, psi -37.5, PINNED).
2026-08-05 14:20:00      outer_fixed313 converges normally (20-27 iterations). At 360 x 96 BOTH converge
2026-08-05 14:20:00      (27 and 36 iterations), so the limit cycle is grid-dependent, not model-dependent.
2026-08-05 14:20:00      The frozen protocol (coupling_max_iters = 200, coupling_tolerance = 1e-6) is kept
2026-08-05 14:20:00      unchanged; the robin runs therefore report picard = 200 with R_p ~ 3e-4.
